Core library for the DonKbot and Open Robotics Platform parts: the o-ring drive wheels, the
shared dimensions and the geometry helpers they use. The upstream LICENSE is copied verbatim
from the pinned commit. nut.scad and the photos are not vendored because nothing in the
catalog uses them.

wedge.scad is deliberately NOT vendored. torus.scad (from chrisspen/openscad-extra, MIT) uses
it, but the copy of wedge.scad in the pinned commit carries a third-party header -
"Copyright 2013 Jonathan Hulka ... GNU General Public License ... version 2 ... or (at your
option) any later version" - which this repository does not redistribute. torus.scad only
calls wedge() from its angle < 360 branch; the catalog's wheels always ask for a full 360
degree torus, so no wedge code is ever reached. OpenSCAD reports the unresolved `use` as a
WARNING when the wheels are rendered, which is expected and harmless (the render succeeds).
The four files are vendored the way dkb_core.scad addresses them, by bare filename, so this
tree's root sits on OPENSCADPATH.

